The skeleton needs a full implementation. Here is how it works:

1. **API**
   - `Palindromes.generate({ minFactor, maxFactor })` checks the range and returns a `Palindromes` instance.
   - If `min > max`, it throws `Error('min must be <= max')`.
   - `minFactor` defaults to `1` if it is not given.

2. **Results**
   - The `smallest` and `largest` getters each return `{ value, factors }`.
   - Each is computed only when first accessed, then cached.
   - If no palindrome product exists, they return `{ value: null, factors: [] }`.
   - Every pair of factors is collected and returned with the smaller factor first, sorted in ascending order.

3. **Efficiency**
   - Checking every product of two 4-digit numbers would be slow, so the searches stop early when they can.
   - **Smallest:** loop `i` upward, with `j` going from `i` upward. A row stops once its product exceeds the best value found so far. The whole search stops once `i * i` exceeds the best value.
   - **Largest:** loop `i` downward, with `j` going from `max` down to `i`. A row stops once its product drops below the best value. The whole search stops once `i * max` is below the best value.
   - Each search continues while products equal the best value, so all factor pairs are found.
   - The palindrome check reverses the digits arithmetically instead of converting the number to a string.

palindrome-products.js
```javascript
//
// Palindrome Products
//

/**
 * Checks whether a non-negative integer reads the same forwards and backwards.
 * @param {number} n
 * @returns {boolean}
 */
const isPalindrome = (n) => {
  if (n < 0) return false;
  let reversed = 0;
  let rest = n;
  while (rest > 0) {
    reversed = reversed * 10 + (rest % 10);
    rest = Math.floor(rest / 10);
  }
  return reversed === n;
};

export class Palindromes {
  constructor(minFactor, maxFactor) {
    this.minFactor = minFactor;
    this.maxFactor = maxFactor;
    this._smallest = null;
    this._largest = null;
  }

  static generate({ minFactor = 1, maxFactor } = {}) {
    if (minFactor > maxFactor) {
      throw new Error('min must be <= max');
    }
    return new Palindromes(minFactor, maxFactor);
  }

  get smallest() {
    if (this._smallest === null) {
      this._smallest = this._findSmallest();
    }
    return this._smallest;
  }

  get largest() {
    if (this._largest === null) {
      this._largest = this._findLargest();
    }
    return this._largest;
  }

  _findSmallest() {
    const min = this.minFactor;
    const max = this.maxFactor;
    let value = null;
    let factors = [];

    for (let i = min; i <= max; i++) {
      // Every product from this row onwards is at least i * i.
      if (value !== null && i * i > value) break;

      for (let j = i; j <= max; j++) {
        const product = i * j;
        // Products only grow as j increases, so nothing better remains in this row.
        if (value !== null && product > value) break;

        if (isPalindrome(product)) {
          if (value === null || product < value) {
            value = product;
            factors = [[i, j]];
          } else {
            // product === value: another factor pair for the same palindrome
            factors.push([i, j]);
          }
        }
      }
    }

    return { value, factors };
  }

  _findLargest() {
    const min = this.minFactor;
    const max = this.maxFactor;
    let value = null;
    let factors = [];

    for (let i = max; i >= min; i--) {
      // Every product from this row onwards is at most i * max.
      if (value !== null && i * max < value) break;

      for (let j = max; j >= i; j--) {
        const product = i * j;
        // Products only shrink as j decreases, so nothing better remains in this row.
        if (value !== null && product < value) break;

        if (isPalindrome(product)) {
          if (value === null || product > value) {
            value = product;
            factors = [[i, j]];
          } else {
            // product === value: another factor pair for the same palindrome
            factors.push([i, j]);
          }
        }
      }
    }

    // Factors were collected from the largest first factor downwards;
    // present them in ascending order.
    factors.reverse();
    return { value, factors };
  }
}
```

